    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n71047" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοσ-ηρός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>diseased,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀστέον νοσηρότερον</span> (v.l.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοσηλ</span>-) <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				50
			</span></i>; <i>unhealthy,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χωρία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					1.6.16
				</span></i>
			; <i>unwholesome,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.974c
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Oct.</u>
				12
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				Comp.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ότερον</span>
			v.l. for
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοσηλ</span>- (q.v.).</div>
